Yellow dragons are stoning resistant because of their acidity. I don't
see any real problem with a yellow draconian being acid-resistant but
not actually acidic.

I'd say that intrinsic magic resistance is more of a worry; getting it
would free up another slot in the AK to use for something else. (I
expect Marvin has ascended an MRless character, but it's essential for
us mortals.)

And, as the race was suggested, I think it's Too Good: cannibalism
isn't penalised heavily enough to deter them from eating a couple of
dragons to fill in intrinsic gaps, just a few points of luck (easily
made back by sacrifice) and aggravate monster (which is mostly
harmless).

The "standard" way to penalise superraces like draconians is to slow
their XL gain. It wouldn't be hard to double the XP requirements for
their levels, but this is really only an early game problem (since
late levels aren't usually acquired by XP), and I think they'd still
be too overpowered in the late game.

